  "metadata": {
    "tags": "UK garage 2-step, bright kalimba lead over a warm rolling sub-bass drop and crisp sampled drum breaks with shuffled hats; 132 BPM, bright bittersweet bounce; airy, intimate female vocal spanning a wide range and climbing into powerful full-voice top-note belts; crisp, clean production.",
    "prompt": "[Intro: kalimba lead, shuffled 2-step hats]\n\n[Verse 1]\nYou print in blue, I print in red\nWe pass the sheet across the bed\nHalf a breath late, half an inch wide\nOur colours never quite collide\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nHold it up to the window light\nNeither of us got it right\n\n[Chorus]\nBut where we miss, a third colour grows\nViolet in the overlap that nobody chose\nOff by a hair, and I like it that way\nMisregistered, we stay\n\n[Bassline Drop]\n\n[Verse 2]\nCoffee rings on the proof we drew\nThe edges ghost where I followed you\nYou lean left and I lean late\nTwo plates turning through one day\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nHold it up to the window light\nNeither of us got it right\n\n[Chorus]\nBut where we miss, a third colour grows\nViolet in the overlap that nobody chose\nOff by a hair, and I like it that way\nMisregistered, we stay\n\n[Bridge]\nIf we lined up perfect we'd be one flat shade\nI'd rather keep the halo the mistake made\n\n[Bassline Drop]\n\n[Final Chorus]\nWhere we miss, a third colour grows\nViolet in the overlap that nobody chose\nOff by a hair, and I like it that way\nMisregistered, we stay\n\n[Outro: solo kalimba fading out]",
